  "body": "Stacked on #1228 (base it on main once #1228 merges; this branch carries #1228's two commits).\nFork synced at v0.18.0.\n\n## What changed\n- #1228 credits a facet edge its whole chord dip when both of its ends lie on a declared hole rim. That left a gap: a hole that is really a coarse polygon, declared or recognized at its corner circle, kept the full credit on its flats. A drill cycle's own rim (tool diameter / 2) left the same gap.\n- `crates/sim/src/verify/solid_index.rs` (`on_rim`): a rim chord now also has to dip at most `RIM_SAG_MAX` (0.05 mm) inside its circle, `r - sqrt(r^2 - l^2/4)`.\n  - A deeper chord counts as a polygon's flat. It gets the 0.01 mm mesh credit, like every off-rim edge.\n  - An octagon on r 5 (flats 0.38 mm deep) or a 16-gon on r 5 (0.096 mm) now convicts against a drill, bore or thread of the corner-circle size.\n- The fix sits in the verifier rather than the recognizer. The hole list is editable data, and the drill's own rim bypasses the recognizer, so the verifier is the one gate every path goes through.\n- Decision: `docs/decisions/1231-rim-sagitta-bound.md` (it also lists what was dropped: inscribed-radius declaration, the STEP `ReducedFidelity` chord, the surface type, a segment-count rule).\n\n## Tests\n- New in `crates/app/tests/hole_wall_chord.rs`:\n  - `a_polygon_declared_at_its_corner_circle_still_convicts_on_its_flats`: 8-gon and 16-gon on r 5, rim declared at r 5; a drill, bore orbit and thread helix each convict. It fails with the bound removed (checked).\n  - `a_small_tessellated_round_hole_keeps_its_rim_credit`: 16-gon r 2 (0.038 mm), a matched 4 mm drill on its rim is clean.\n- Quick gate `cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/issue/1217-chord-dip-excuse` on the final head: green (sim lib, midmove_pose, posed_rapids, motion solid_law, app hole_wall_chord, probe_reach, real_tip_contour, tool_body_drill_probe).\n- Also run by hand, all green:\n  - app `solid_law_goldens` (drill_plate, tap_plate), `golden_cl`, `bore_facet_sagitta`, `solid_law`, `conformance`, `fanuc_post`;\n  - `operations` drill tests, including `drill_op_recognizes_from_the_model_then_machines_clean`.\n- Clippy `-D warnings` on camcraft-sim and camcraft-app (all targets): clean.\n- No golden or snapshot changed.\n\n## Not exercised\n- Real coarse STL exports: any round hole that dips more than 0.05 mm is now judged as a polygon. That is a refusal, not a pass.\n- The batch and release tiers.\n\nChangelog: Verify: a polygonal hole declared or drilled at its corner circle no longer has its flats excused; a chord counts as round-hole tessellation only when it dips at most 0.05 mm (#1231)\n\nEffort: high (no escalation)\n\nFixes #1231\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
